 1067 "Introduction" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186180774 #edb/ref 1064 "The **quotient** of two numbers means that we need to divide the first number by the second number.\n\nFor example, \"the quotient of $x$ and two\" means the same thing as \"$x$ divided by two\" and can be written as either expression below:\n\n$$\n\\dfrac{x}{2} ,\\qquad x \\div 2 \\, .\n$$\n\nIn algebra, we prefer to represent division using the fraction bar instead of the ($\\div$) symbol." #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186180774 #edb/ref 1065 8168 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186180774 #edb/ref 1066 #uuid "966707d2-a5e7-5ce1-a0b4-1c2991c80e3d" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186180774 #edb/ref 1067 "The Division Sign in Algebra" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186443550 #edb/ref 1080 "3\\cdot (3+a)" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186443550 #edb/ref 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045498 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186443550 #edb/ref 1083 #uuid "04502abf-d30a-536a-91df-b4f259198cbc" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186443551 #edb/ref 1080 "a\\cdot (3-a)" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186443551 #edb/ref 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045498 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186443551 #edb/ref 1083 #uuid "098a42b2-f9f6-59cf-8afe-73f54612025a" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186443552 #edb/ref 1080 "30w" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186443552 #edb/ref 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045498 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186443552 #edb/ref 1083 #uuid "14207910-bc3d-5531-8c71-def14534c5c9" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186443553 #edb/ref 1080 "4+x" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186443553 #edb/ref 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045498 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186443553 #edb/ref 1083 #uuid "1c85e377-c6c4-5da5-9c0b-11a2bd86cad2" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186443554 #edb/ref 1080 "3a" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186443554 #edb/ref 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045498 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186443554 #edb/ref 1083 #uuid "20a7d5c1-5cae-5ede-9f9f-7716fe5947a5" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186443555 #edb/ref 1080 "\\frac