se can be written as\n\n$$\na\\cdot (3+a).\n$$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186443593 #edb/ref 1068 #edb/ref 17592186443584 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186443593 #edb/ref 1069 "q-27483" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186443593 #edb/ref 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045486 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186443593 #edb/ref 1071 "The algebraic expression $4w-3$ can be translated into a sentence as" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186443593 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "4b801c4c-53a9-5277-82f6-60fd8ea8ed73" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186443593 #edb/ref 1074 "The first term of the expression is $4w$ and this can be written as \"four times a number\".\n\nSince we have the subtraction $4w-3$, the whole expression can be written as \"the difference between four times a number and three\"." #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186443594 #edb/ref 1068 #edb/ref 17592186443582 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186443594 #edb/ref 1069 "q-21264" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186443594 #edb/ref 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045487 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186443594 #edb/ref 1071 "Translate the phrase \"one-quarter of a number minus three-sevenths of another number\" into an algebraic expression." #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186443594 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "5efd65b1-9dc8-5a12-83d6-fd8f864d64db" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186443594 #edb/ref 1074 "If we denote our first number by $x$ and our second number by $y$, then we can write \"one-quarter of a number \" as\n\n$$\n\\frac{1}{4}x\n$$\n\nand \"three-sevenths of a second number\" as\n\n$$\n\\frac{3}{7}y.\n$$\n\nSo, the whole sentence is \n\n$$\n\\frac{1}{4}x-\\frac{3}{7}y.\n$$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186443595 #edb/ref 1068 #edb/ref 17592186443585 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186443595 #edb/ref 1069 "q-184029" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186443595 #edb/ref 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045485 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186443595 #edb/ref 1071 "Translate the following phrase into an algebraic expression: \"A quarter of a number.\"\n\nUse the letter $y$ to represent the unknown number.\n\n{{field-1}}" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186443595 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "74b51296-c7b7-5c19-8f08-00846b0aaa79" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186443595 #edb/ref 1074 "If we denote our number by $y,$ then the phrase can be written as $\\frac{1}{4}y.$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186443596 #edb/ref 1068 #edb/ref 17592186443588 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186443596 #edb/ref 1069 "q-184024" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186443596 #edb/ref 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045487 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186443596 #edb/ref 1071 "Translate the following phrase into an algebraic expression: \"$20$ minus five times a number.\"\n\nUse the letter $w$ to represent the unknown number.\n\n{{field-1}}" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186443596 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "7e58b785-f5f2-5a07-a9a0-a68f78076577" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186443596 #edb/ref 1074 "If we denote our number by $w$, then \"five times a number'' can be written as\n\n$$\n5w.\n$$\n\nSo, the whole phrase can be written as\n\n$$\n20-5w.\n$$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186443597 #edb/ref 1068 #edb/ref 17592186443587 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186443597 #edb/ref 1069 "q-171407" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186443597 #edb/ref 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045485 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186443597 #edb/ref 1071 "Translate the following phrase into an algebraic expression: \"Two-thirds of a number.\"\n\nUse the letter $k$ to represent the unknown number.\n\n{{field-1}}" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186443597 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "9993235d-0a25-5a28-9986-8e8c61052303" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186443597 #edb/ref 1074 "If we denote our number by $k,$ then the phrase can be written as $\\frac{2}{3}k.$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186443598 #edb/ref 1068 #edb/ref 17592186443580 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186443598 #edb/ref 1069 "q-54498" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186443598 #edb/ref 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045485 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186443598 #edb/ref 1071 "Write \"the quotient of a number and three\" as an algebraic expression." #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186443598 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "cc4c452a-9b60-579e-b407-bfc2250db098" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186443598 #edb/ref 1074 "\"The quotient of a number and three\" means the same thing as \"a number divided by three.\" \n\nIf we call our number $n$, then we can express this mathematically as $\\frac{n}{3}.$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186443599 #edb/ref 1068 #edb/ref 17592186443586 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186443599 #edb/ref 1069 "q-184026" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186443599 #edb/ref 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045485 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186443599 #edb/ref 1071 "Translate the following phrase into an algebraic expression: \"The quotient of twenty and a number.\"\n\nUse the letter $h$ to represent the unknown number.\n\n{{field-1}}" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186443599 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "e410a5c3-45c2-5472-8881-f44191caa0a7" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186443599 #edb/ref 1074 "If we denote our number by $h,$ we can write \"the quotient of twenty and a number\" as $\\frac{20}{h}.$" #edb/ref 17592186045417]}
